A||N||4||mindscape||While it is apart...||||1||
Z||000000||mindscape||07-12-2001||11:35 PM||||A couple of weeks ago my 1988 Fiero GT died.<P>Currently it is apart... are there any recommendations as to things to do while it is in this condition; modifications, enhancements, or . . . <P>The cross over pipe was broken at the coupler.  It has been welded, but what can be used as a replacement heat shield?<P>What can be used to re-wrap the wiring harness; as the current reflective tape is falling off.<P>Fuel injector service?  Who?  Where?  How much?<P>Recommendations on cleaning aluminum parts?<P>Molly versus standard rings?||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||07-12-2001||11:51 PM||||Can't give ya many suggestions about that other stuff, but I ordered a roll of heat reflective tape from summit racing.  The stuff is especially made for wrapping wiring harnesses.  I believe they also have heat blankets that you can cut to fit, if you need to replace some of those.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||07-13-2001||12:00 AM||||Might think about porting the exhaust manifolds, if they're coming off anyway.    ||||reg||3
Z||000003||Leadfoot||07-13-2001||10:29 AM||||Can't help you with the rest but I do know how to get all that carbon gunk off the aluminum parts quick and easy.  I used aircraft paint stripper (available at pep boys).  It works like a charm.  Wear some good thick nylon gloves and goggles.  Wash all the parts with mineral spirits when you are done.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||07-13-2001||11:13 AM||||moly rings are ok but expect to use some oil, <A HREF="http://www.Thermotec.com" TARGET=_blank>www.Thermotec.com</A>  the header wrap and wiring reflective tape they are talking aobut.. i use it a lot.. greatest thing since sliced bread. ||||reg||1
